{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Whom He blessed.</b> For HaShem blessed Israel; therefore he will be a blessing. Then He will bless each one of these three:" "<b>Blessed be My people.</b> Because they will make an altar to HaShem publicly, He called them My people." "<b>And the work of My hands.</b> That there are in them a few people who will recognize the deed of HaShem." "<b>And My inheritance.</b> That they are His inheritance forever, for Assyria and Egypt are like an accident compared to them. And the translator [Targum] said: Blessed be My people who are in Egypt."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:23.622349479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}